    "title": "A Call for Fiscal Accountability - NewsBreak",
    "text": "11 hours ago While property taxes continue to rise across municipalities—often by double-digit percentages the promised improvements to public infrastructure and education remain largely unmet. Citizens are navigating deteriorating roads and under-resourced classrooms despite increased financial contributions. This disconnect raises a critical question of accountability:\nAre public funds being allocated with transparency, efficiency, and measurable impact?\nTaxation must be paired with tangible outcomes. Without visible progress, trust in governance erodes. It is not enough to collect more—we must ensure that every dollar serves the public good with integrity and clarity.",
